; e106_reject_list_cap.chiral — E106 conformance: REJECTION 1 of 4.
;
; Storing a linear cap (an `Env` porttype) in the UNRESTRICTED `List` is rejected
; by construction: `List`'s `hd` field is `(hd A)` (quantity ω, prelude.chiral:19),
; and an unrestricted field could be dropped or duplicated — which would drop or
; double-close the cap. This is WHY E106 builds a `1`-fielded `SockVec` instead
; of reusing `List`. Expected B1 verdict: `load: linear field hd`.
(import "prelude/prelude")
(import "ports/ports")

(def bad (-> (1 a Env) (List Env))
  (lam (a) (cons a nil)))
